# Build artifacts
target/
*.jar
*.class
test/reports

# Clojure cache
.cpcache/
.nrepl-port
# clj-kondo: keep config.edn and hooks/ tracked — both are hand-written, and a
# blanket **/.clj-kondo/ previously swallowed committed hooks.
#
# .cache/ and imports/ are generated and are not. imports/ holds configs kondo
# copies out of dependency jars: it has never been tracked, it is regenerated on
# demand, and it changes with every dependency upgrade with nobody maintaining
# it. Measured on the full source tree, present or absent, it changes no lint
# result — so tracking it would add churn and a permanently dirty `git status`
# for no signal. CI never generates it either, so ignoring it is also what keeps
# local and CI linting the same inputs.
**/.clj-kondo/.cache/
**/.clj-kondo/imports/
.lsp

